## Skills

Apply on every task, no exceptions. Load each skill on demand (by name or
link); this file never `@`-imports a skill, so none loads into context
automatically:

<!-- harness: never render an `@` import of a skill in this file. -->
- `hexagonal-architecture` — dependencies point inward; the domain references
  no framework; adapters translate and classify; adapters are constructed only
  at the composition root. **This is fixed, not a preference.**
- `tdd` — write the failing test first, **watch it fail** for the expected
  reason (it compiles, runs and fails), then write the minimum code to pass.
  Every behaviour change and every bug fix, however small.
- `separation-of-concerns` — which layer owns a piece of logic, and why.
- `extract-til-you-drop` — decompose every function until no further
  intention-revealing extraction remains. New code, not just refactors.

