### Rules that survive every refactor

- Dispatch means an Agent tool call. Doing a subagent's work inline is not
  dispatch.
- Never advance the chain on a receipt that isn't `STATUS: done`.
- Post a one-line dispatch note before each agent and its receipt after — a
  subagent's output is invisible to the user otherwise.
- Never give a verify agent a verdict; give it scope.
- Each implement agent edits at most its file cap per invocation
  ({{FILE_CAPS}}).
- There is no meta-orchestrator subagent. The root walks the graph itself.

